    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;6.03</strong> Histological criteria for grading appendiceal primary mucinous tumours, including mucinous neoplasms and adenocarcinomas, and their peritoneal metastases</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Reetesh K. Pai",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 100.0%; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.12%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"8%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Tumour grade</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Primary appendiceal mucinous tumour terminology</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histological criteria in the primary tumour</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Terminology for potential peritoneal metastasis</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Grading criteria for peritoneal metastases<sup>a</sup></span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.12%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"8%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Low-grade appendiceal mucinous neoplasm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Circumferential proliferation of mucinous epithelium with low-grade cytological features and pushing, diverticulum-like extension into or through the wall</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Low-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Hypocellular mucinous deposits</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Neoplastic epithelium with low-grade cytological features</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">No infiltrative-type invasion</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.12%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"8%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">2</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-grade appendiceal mucinous neoplasm</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Circumferential proliferation of mucinous epithelium with high-grade cytological features and pushing, diverticulum-like extension into or through the wall</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">High-grade cytological features involving &ge;&nbsp;10% of tumour epithelium</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Hypercellular mucinous deposits as judged at 20&times; magnification typically present</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Infiltrative-type invasion typically present and characterized by angulated glands in a desmoplastic stroma, or numerous small mucin pools containing clusters of tumour cells</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Mucinous adenocarcinoma</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Malignant glands with infiltrative invasion with extracellular mucin composing &gt;&nbsp;50% of the tumour</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.12%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"8%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Mucinous adenocarcinoma with signet-ring cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Malignant glands with infiltrative invasion and with signet-ring cells making up &ge;&nbsp;10% of tumour epithelium<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">High-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei with signet-ring cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Infiltrative signet-ring cells with desmoplasia or signet-ring cells floating in mucin</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Signet-ring cells involve &ge;&nbsp;10% of tumour epithelium<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Signet-ring cell adenocarcinoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 22.96%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210040711;\">Tumour composed of &gt;&nbsp;50% signet-ring cells<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Generally, the grade of the appendiceal mucinous tumour and the peritoneal mucinous tumour are concordant. Rarely, they are discordant. In discordant cases, the grade of the appendiceal and peritoneal tumour deposits should be separately reported. The grade of the peritoneal tumour has a greater effect on prognosis than that of the appendiceal primary tumour. <sup>b</sup>The presence of signet-ring cells is prognostically significant even if they do not constitute 50% of the tumour required to be classified as a signet-ring cell adenocarcinoma. Tumours composed of &lt;&nbsp;50% signet-ring cells qualify as grade&nbsp;3 mucinous adenocarcinoma, and a notation of signet-ring cells being present is appropriate. Signet-ring cells in mucin must be distinguished from degenerate tumour cells in the mucin (pseudo&ndash;signet-ring cells), and therefore &ge;&nbsp;10% of the tumour epithelium should be signet-ring cells to be classified as grade&nbsp;3.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
